---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
const updated = 'June 28, 2026';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Delete Your Account"
  updated={updated}
  path="/delete-account"
  description="How to delete your Stride account and all associated data — in-app in seconds, or by email request."
>
  <p>You can delete your <strong>Stride</strong> account and all of its data at any time. Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.</p>

  <h2>Option 1 — Delete in the app (instant)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open the Stride app.</li>
    <li>Go to <strong>Profile → Settings → Delete account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Confirm. Your account and data are removed immediately.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Option 2 — Request deletion by email</h2>
  <p>If you can’t access the app, email <a href="mailto:hello@striderunning.run">hello@striderunning.run</a> from the email address on your Stride account, with the subject <strong>“Delete my account”</strong>. We’ll verify ownership and delete your account within <strong>30 days</strong> (usually much sooner).</p>

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <p>Deleting your account permanently removes your profile and personal data, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your email, username, display name, avatar, bio, gender, date of birth and settings</li>
    <li>All of your runs, routes, GPS/activity data and claimed territory</li>
    <li>Your posts, comments, photos, kudos, clubs, events and challenges</li>
    <li>Your followers/following connections and safety contacts</li>
    <li>Any health-derived data and your push notification token</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>Your data is removed from our production systems immediately. Residual copies may remain in encrypted backups within their normal rotation period (up to ~30 days), after which they are permanently overwritten. We retain nothing required only for the deleted account beyond this window, except where the law requires us to keep limited records.</p>

  <p>For full details on how we handle your data, see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
